	<description>Loudmouthed, redheaded Cee Cee Bloom has her sights set on Hollywood. Bertie White, quiet and conservative, dreams of getting married and having children. In 1951, their childhood worlds collide in Atlantic City. Keeping in touch as pen pals, they reunite over the years ... always near the ocean.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Powerful and moving, this novel follows Cee Cee and Bertie's extraordinary friendship over the course of thirty years as they transform from adolescents into adults. A bestselling novel that became a hugely successful film, &lt;em&gt;Beaches&lt;/em&gt; is funny, heartbreaking, and a tale that should be a part of every woman's library.</description>
